WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.230
- [Instructor] We have three
different pictures here,

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.990
and my question to get us warmed up

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:09.990
is which of these could
represent 20 divided by four?

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.100
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.800
All right, so let's go
through each of these.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.120
And, actually, let's think about

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.830
what each of them could represent.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.030
So how many total circles
do we have in this picture

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:24.970
right over here?

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:28.620
Let's see, we have one, two, three, four,

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.840
and then we have four groups of four.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.620
So four, eight, 12, 16.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.230
So this looks like 16 circles.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.070
16 circles divided into,

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.930
we could do it as divided
into groups of four,

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.470
or we could actually also view it

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.780
as divided into four equal groups,

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.440
because both of those are true.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.620
And we see that that is
going to be equal to four.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.690
So this one over here,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.510
it's really representing
16 divided by four,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.790
not 20 divided by four.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.360
Now, what about this one?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.060
Let's see, here, it looks
like we have one, two,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.970
three, four, five groups

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.140
of one, two, three, four, five.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:14.180
So this looks like 25 circles

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.700
divided into groups of five,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.960
or divided into five equals groups,

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.270
which is, of course, equal to five.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:26.193
So this is 25 divided by
five, not 20 divided by four.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.910
Now, but what about this one?

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:32.330
So let's see, we have one,
two, three, four, five,

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:37.330
and we have, one, two,
three, four groups of five.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.970
So five, 10, 15, 20.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.400
So we definitely have 20 circles there.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.810
And we have divided it
into four equal groups.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.180
We have divided it into four equal groups,

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.220
and so that's exactly
what we're talking about,

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.510
or what we started talking about.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.080
This is 20 divided by four.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.963
And you can see, when you take 20

00:01:54.963 --> 00:01:58.280
and divide it into four equal groups,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.280
then you get one, two, three,
four, five circles per group.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.013
And we're done.

